reviews_attraction.text:
Get there early in the day and you will find parking near the gift shop entry, else you must park in their lot across the street from the entry area.

There is a very large gift shop and in the right hand center is the desk for obtaining tour tickets.  Check the Internet for discount coupons and prices as these range from $32 for Seniors to $40 regular Adult.  {a little steep, but worth the cost for a visit once every 40 years}..

There is a snack-bar restaurant where you can obtain a decent lunch or a cup of coffee.  There are tons of things to see on a self-tour of the grounds and several buildings are open.  You will be photographed upon presenting your ticket at the entry to the home {this is a money making enterprise as the photos are for sale} and for the rifleman there is a small but free Winchester Arms museum.

There are more than one tour, we took the basic and enjoyed the antics and stories of our informative guide.  Do not be afraid to ask questions, he or she will be very happy to know you are interested in the answers {giving the same spiel nine times a day can become monotonous}

You are allowed to take pictures in the gift shop and on the beautiful grounds, but NOT in the building itself.  If you like beauty and interesting architecture, then you will be taking many pictures.

Allow three to four hours for your visit and then proceed to the San Jose / Sunnyvale Rose Garden; followed by an afternoon four hours at the Rosicrucian Museum that is at 1660 Park Ave. {short drive away}
